    <!-- v1.3.3: Automation / auto-apply on reboot -->
    <string name="automation">Automation</string>
    <string name="auto_apply_on_reboot">Auto-apply settings on reboot</string>
    <string name="auto_apply_hint_label">How it works</string>
    <string name="auto_apply_hint_value">Settings are saved automatically every time you change a toggle. They are re-applied whenever the carrier config may have been reset: after a reboot, after an app update, and when the system reloads carrier settings.\n\nThe re-apply is queued as persistent background work and runs the moment Shizuku becomes reachable — seconds after boot or hours later, whenever you start it. Nothing is applied twice: if the live config already matches, IMS is left alone.\n\nShizuku must be running for this to happen. Without root it does not start by itself; the usual setup is Developer Options → Wireless Debugging plus the start-on-boot option in Shizuku itself. No root required.</string>

